<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-bs-theme="dark">

<head>
  <%- include('partials/head', {
    title: 'Guides - Countic',
    description: 'Set up YouTube, Twitch or Kick counters in Discord voice channels with Countic. One command builds a live stats panel.',
    canonicalPath: '/guide',
  }); %>
</head>

<body id="top" class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100">

  <%- include('partials/header', { active: 'guide' }); %>

  <main class="container my-5">
    <%
      const platforms = [
        {
          id: 'youtube',
          name: 'YouTube',
          icon: '/img/youtube.webp',
          intro: 'Run <code>/setup</code>, pick <strong>youtube</strong> as the platform and paste your channel in the channel option. A URL, an @handle or the bare <code>UC...</code> channel ID all work, for example <code>youtube.com/@yourchannel</code> or <code>@yourchannel</code>.',
          example: '/setup platform:youtube channel:https://www.youtube.com/@yourchannel',
          counters: [
            'the category <code>[name] • YouTube</code>, named after the tracked channel',
            '<code>Subs: [subs]</code> with the live subscriber count',
            '<code>Views: [views]</code> with the total view count',
            '<code>Videos: [videos]</code> with the total video count',
          ],
          after: 'All three counters refresh every hour on a fixed schedule. YouTube reports abbreviated subscriber counts, Countic renders them exactly as YouTube provides them.',
        },
        {
          id: 'twitch',
          name: 'Twitch',
          icon: '/img/twitch.webp',
          intro: 'Run <code>/setup</code>, pick <strong>twitch</strong> as the platform and enter the Twitch account in the channel option. The username works, and so do a <code>twitch.tv/yourusername</code> link or <code>@yourusername</code>. Twitch usernames are 3 to 25 letters, numbers and underscores.',
          example: '/setup platform:twitch channel:yourusername',
          counters: [
            'the category <code>[name] • Twitch</code>, named after the tracked account',
            '<code>Followers: [followers]</code> with the follower count',
            '<code>Viewers: [viewers]</code> with the current viewer count',
          ],
          after: 'Both counters refresh every 15 minutes, so viewer counts stay close to live. While the stream is offline the viewers counter shows <strong>Offline</strong> and the followers counter keeps counting.',
        },
        {
          id: 'kick',
          name: 'Kick',
          icon: '/img/kick.png',
          intro: 'Run <code>/setup</code>, pick <strong>kick</strong> as the platform and enter the Kick account in the channel option. The username works, and so do a <code>kick.com/yourusername</code> link or <code>@yourusername</code>. Kick usernames are 2 to 25 letters, numbers and underscores.',
          example: '/setup platform:kick channel:yourusername',
          counters: [
            'the category <code>[name] • Kick</code>, named after the tracked account',
            '<code>Followers: [followers]</code> with the follower count',
            '<code>Viewers: [viewers]</code> with the current viewer count',
          ],
          after: 'Both counters refresh every 15 minutes. While the stream is offline the viewers counter shows <strong>Offline</strong> and the followers counter keeps counting.',
        },
      ];
      const selected = platforms.find((entry) => entry.id === platformId) ?? platforms[0];
    %>

    <h1 class="text-center mb-4">Guides</h1>
    <p class="lead text-center">Live stats as voice channels in your server, one command per platform. Pick
      yours below.</p>

    <section class="my-4">
      <h2>Step 1 - Invite the Bot</h2>
      <p><a href="/add" class="text-decoration-none fw-bold text-primary-emphasis border-bottom">Invite Countic</a> to your server and keep the
        <strong>Manage Channels</strong> permission enabled for it. That is the only permission Countic needs,
        it creates, renames and deletes voice channels. Managing the panel
        later needs the same permission for you.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <ul class="nav nav-pills justify-content-center gap-2 my-4" role="tablist" aria-label="Pick a platform">
      <% platforms.forEach((entry) => { %>
      <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
        <button
          id="tab-<%= entry.id %>"
          class="nav-link pill-<%= entry.id %><%= entry.id === selected.id ? ' active' : '' %>"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          data-bs-toggle="tab"
          data-bs-target="#pane-<%= entry.id %>"
          aria-selected="<%= entry.id === selected.id %>"
          aria-controls="pane-<%= entry.id %>"
        >
          <img src="<%= entry.icon %>" width="20" height="20" alt="" class="me-2">
          <%= entry.name %>
        </button>
      </li>
      <% }); %>
    </ul>

    <div class="tab-content">
      <% platforms.forEach((entry) => { %>
      <div
        class="tab-pane fade<%= entry.id === selected.id ? ' show active' : '' %>"
        id="pane-<%= entry.id %>"
        role="tabpanel"
        aria-labelledby="tab-<%= entry.id %>"
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <h2 class="h4">Step 2 - Run /setup</h2>
        <p><%- entry.intro %></p>
        <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded border"><%= entry.example %></pre>
        <p>Countic creates:</p>
        <ul>
          <% entry.counters.forEach((counter) => { %>
          <li><%- counter %></li>
          <% }); %>
        </ul>
        <p>Fresh counters start as <code>...</code> and fill with real numbers on the first update pass, usually
          within a couple of minutes. <%- entry.after %></p>
      </div>
      <% }); %>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <section class="my-4">
      <h2>Step 3 - Manage Your Panel</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>/set-channel</code> points the panel at a different source. The counters keep their names and
          formats and pick up the new source on the next update pass, usually within a couple of minutes.</li>
        <li><code>/panel status</code> shows every counter with its current name, its state and the last update.
          Without a platform it summarizes all panels at once, and a counter that stopped working carries the
          recorded reason, like a deleted channel or missing permissions.</li>
        <li><code>/panel delete</code> removes a panel after a confirmation, deleting the category, the counter
          channels and the stored settings. With the optional counter option it removes a single counter
          instead.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section class="my-4">
      <h2>Step 4 - Customize the Names</h2>
      <p>Run <code>/customize template</code>, pick a counter and edit the template in the dialog, prefilled
        with the current name. Every stat counter must contain its own placeholder, <code>[subs]</code>,
        <code>[views]</code>, <code>[videos]</code>, <code>[followers]</code> or <code>[viewers]</code>,
        surrounded by whatever text you like. Example template: <code>Subs: [subs]</code>. Leaving the dialog
        empty resets the counter to its default name.</p>
      <p>The category is named with <code>[name]</code> plus plain text, like <code>[name] • My Community</code>.
        <code>[name]</code> is optional, so plain text alone works too, for example <code>My Community</code> keeps a
        fixed label that no longer follows channel renames. Stat placeholders are not allowed in the category.</p>
      <p><code>/customize format</code> switches a counter between compact (<code>1.23M</code>) and full
        (<code>1,230,000</code>) numbers. Subscriber and follower counters start compact, the rest starts full,
        and the separators follow the language set in your Discord server settings, so a Turkish server sees
        <code>1,23M</code> where an English server sees <code>1.23M</code>.</p>
      <p><code>/customize view</code> lists every counter of a panel with its template, a rendered preview and
        any recorded problem.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section class="my-4">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Source not found?</strong> Use the exact username or paste the full channel URL, links and
          handles resolve.</li>
        <li><strong>Counters not updating?</strong> Run <code>/panel status</code>, it names the reason per
          counter. Fix the cause and run <code>/setup</code> again, your templates are kept.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer'); %>
</body>

</html>
